<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cancho Roano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th–5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cancho Roano is an archaeological site near Zalamea de la Serena in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/extremadura">Extremadura</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Its building, dating from about the 6th to the late 5th century BCE, is interpreted as a palace-sanctuary of the late Tartessian world and was deliberately burned and buried when it was abandoned. Finds of Greek pottery, jewellery and weapons show the links of inland elites with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cancho-roano.jpg" alt="Cancho Roano" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Axel Cotón Gutiérrez · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Centro_de_Interpretaci%C3%B3n_del_Yacimiento_de_Cancho_Roano._Paneles_informativos_I_06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
